                <pb facs="0540" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7409a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Neville</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-20T16:00:00-05:00">November 20, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. Press despatches from Tokyo state that Foreign Office has issued denial that
                    “the Japanese Government was in any way responsible for the autonomy movement”
                    in North China.</p>
                <p>Please cable text of such statement if issued and texts of other official
                    Japanese statements relative to North China situation if and when made.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
